%% section: Restart behavior
%% caption: Restart, backoff and the rate limit
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Activating
    Activating --> Active: started
    Active --> Failed: non-zero exit or watchdog
    Failed --> Activating: Restart= policy, after RestartSec
    Activating --> RateLimited: StartLimitBurst exceeded in StartLimitIntervalSec
    RateLimited --> [*]: systemd gives up — the unit stays failed
    Active --> Deactivating: stop
    Deactivating --> [*]
    note right of RateLimited
        The rate limit is what stops a crash loop
        consuming the box. It also means a real
        outage needs `systemctl reset-failed`.
    end note
